---
title: point_validity_check (EIP-7951)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> q_check_bounds_x : receive (qx, qy)
    q_check_bounds_x --> q_check_bounds_y : 0 <= qx < p
    q_check_bounds_x --> q_invalid : qx >= p
    q_check_bounds_y --> q_check_inf : 0 <= qy < p
    q_check_bounds_y --> q_invalid : qy >= p
    q_check_inf --> q_compute_lhs : (qx, qy) != (0, 0)
    q_check_inf --> q_invalid : (qx, qy) == (0, 0)
    q_compute_lhs --> q_compute_rhs : lhs = qy^2 (mod p)
    q_compute_rhs --> q_compare : rhs = qx^3 + a*qx + b (mod p)
    q_compare --> q_valid : lhs == rhs
    q_compare --> q_invalid : lhs != rhs
    q_valid --> [*] : point is valid
    q_invalid --> [*] : point is invalid

    note right of q_check_inf
        INV-013: (0, 0) is not on secp256r1, used as point-at-infinity encoding
    end note

    note right of q_compute_rhs
        INV-014: Curve equation uses parameters a, b from NIST SP 800-186
        INV-015: All arithmetic is modular over field Fp
    end note
